From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: slothfulchat <patches@slothfulchat.invalid>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 23:24:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 82/82] web-app: unify the composer link-preview states into
 one card
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The link-preview affordance's states looked like three unrelated widgets:
an idle skeleton card, a spinner-in-a-bar while generating, and a plain
text bar for the "needs a bridge with unfurl enabled" error. Now one
card-shaped skeleton carries all three (#64):

- idle: the dashed skeleton card, as before
- loading: the same card with the border gone solid and a shimmer sweeping
  the placeholder bars/thumbnail (disabled under prefers-reduced-motion) —
  the placeholder reads as "filling in" rather than being replaced
- unavailable: the same card greyed out ("couldn't fill in"), with the
  explanation in the hint line below, where the idle hint sits

The loading/unavailable phases now carry the host so the card keeps
showing it across the idle → loading → error transitions; since all three
states render the same DOM, they morph in place (a 0.2s ease on the
border/opacity cues) instead of swapping components. The ready state is
unchanged. The spinner bar styles (.bar/.barLabel/.linkIcon) are gone.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
